```

`image_contents` is assigned across roughly fifteen lines, including a deliberate single-black-pixel fallback with an explanatory comment, and is then referenced nowhere. Grep confirms the only occurrences are the three assignments.

## Effect

The visual chat feature is inert. A user attaches an image, the UI accepts it, and the request that reaches `/api/chat/visual` is indistinguishable from a plain text question. The reply is plausible — the backend answers the text — so the failure is silent rather than obvious.

## Why nothing caught it

No test covers `sendVisualMessage`, and the E2E smoke exercises `/api/chat/service`, not `/api/chat/visual`. The request succeeds and returns 200, so every layer reports success.

## Suggested fix

Include the image in the body, and add a test asserting the payload sent to `/api/chat/visual` contains the image data when `turn.image` is set. The test should fail against the current code.

Worth confirming what shape the endpoint expects before choosing the key name — the black-pixel fallback suggests the original contract keyed by data-URL prefix, which is unusual and may itself be wrong.

